  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Matt Wilkinson threw five scoreless innings and the Giants managed only one run against him.",
    "what_this_means": "This is what happens when pitching does its job but offense can't match it. Wilkinson was excellent. Five innings, no runs, six strikeouts. And the Giants had him right where they needed. They scored once in six innings and then the bullpen imploded. Seymour gave up a run without getting an out. Hentges came in and gave up another. Smith got the third. Three relievers, three runs, 2.3 innings. The Dodgers took a 1-3 lead by the seventh and it held. The Giants got base runners. They were on base in that first inning when they scored. But they couldn't make it matter beyond that. Good pitching is only half the equation when you're trying to catch a team 32 games back. The other half has to produce.",
    "what_to_watch": "Minnesota visits tonight with Zebby Matthews on the mound for the Twins. Matthews has a 4.74 ERA this season. The kind of matchup where the Giants can't afford another two-hit outing.",
